  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GOVERNING MEASUREMENT. docs/measurements/0001-taint-flow-precision.md puts taint-flow precision at ~41% population-weighted across six real repositories. Per WI-sivuz's PRE-REGISTERED decision bands -- named before any interval was computed, so the interval cannot be used to move them -- that is the <50% band: \"precision is the headline problem and recall work should stop until it is understood.\"\n\nP2 -> P1. PROMOTED. Under the <50% band the precision mechanisms are the priority, and this is the largest one the measurement identifies. From its consequence 4:\n\n  \"env_read -> host_secret is doing more work than the name admits. The Go catalogue's env_read includes os.Getwd, os.Executable, os.Hostname and runtime.GOOS; the JavaScript one includes navigator.platform and window.screen. Calling all of that a SECRET is why host-secret-* claims carry 48 OF THE 85 ADJUDICATED FLOWS at 22.9% PRECISION between them. A vocabulary question, not a per-row edit.\"\n\n48 of 85 flows at 22.9% is the single biggest precision lever named anywhere in the measurement, and this item was at RANK 75 of 227 while the recall fixes it should precede were at ranks 10 and 11. That inversion is what this promotion corrects."  # 1ae0
